; RPZ policy zone with IPv6 rpz-ip triggers, owner names in the reversed,
; prefix-first RPZ form:
;
;   128.1.1.1.1.zz.1.db8.2001  <-> 2001:db8:1:0:1:1:1:1  (single isolated zero)
;   128.zz.1.1.1.1.1.db8.2001  <-> 2001:db8:1:1:1:1:1:0  (single trailing zero)
;   128.1.1.1.1.zz.db8.2001    <-> 2001:db8:0:0:1:1:1:1  (two consecutive zeros)
;
; Each rule maps to "CNAME ." (the RPZ NXDOMAIN action).  The two single-zero
; rules use "zz" for a single isolated zero group, which is not the canonical
; form ip2name() generates (a single zero group renders as ".0").  They load
; with a non-canonical-name warning; the resolver still enforces them by
; retrying the policy lookup under the "zz" spelling when the canonical lookup
; misses.  The two-consecutive-zeros rule is canonical and matches directly.

$TTL 300
@		IN SOA	ns2.lab. hostmaster.lab. ( 1 3600 1200 604800 60 )
@		IN NS	ns2.lab.

128.1.1.1.1.zz.1.db8.2001.rpz-ip	IN CNAME .
128.zz.1.1.1.1.1.db8.2001.rpz-ip	IN CNAME .
128.1.1.1.1.zz.db8.2001.rpz-ip		IN CNAME .
